# Overview

Greetings, reader with a named footnote<sup><a id="fnr.note" class="footref" href="#fn.note" role="doc-backlink">1</a></sup> and another reference<sup><a id="fnr.note.1" class="footref" href="#fn.note" role="doc-backlink">1</a></sup>. Macro arguments: one|; extra arguments: [one].

Safe links: [A label with ]( and \`backtick\` | pipe](https://example.test/path?q=a&b=c) and [section link](#details).

Raw HTML-like text in a literal block:

```
<em>literal HTML</em>
```

This line has a tab between these words: before and after.


<a id="details"></a>

# Detail

The local fragment destination is safe.

## Footnotes

<sup><a id="fn.1" class="footnum" href="#fnr.1">1</a></sup> One definition serves both references.